## Registry navbar icon opens Browse/Bridges modal

Context: Registry is no longer a full page with a left sidebar and dropdown
menu. The navbar now shows a large archive icon only; click opens a modal
with Create a New Domain plus Browse and Bridges tabs. Load Domain was
removed from this entry point.

Changes:

1. `src/front/config/menu_config.json`
   Marked Registry as `navbar_modal`; cleared dropdown actions/groups.
2. `src/front/templates/base.html`
   Icon-only Registry toggle; includes modal + registry CSS/JS globally.
3. `src/front/templates/partials/layout/registry_modal.html` (new)
   Modal with Create a New Domain, Browse and Bridges tabs.
4. `src/front/static/global/js/registry-modal.js` +
   `src/front/static/global/css/registry-modal.css` (new)
   Open/close wiring, tab → load events, `?open=registry` deep link.
5. `src/front/routes/registry.py`
   `GET /registry/` redirects to `/?open=registry`.
6. `src/front/templates/registry.html`
   Deleted — page replaced by the modal.
7. `src/front/templates/partials/registry/_registry_domains.html`
   Removed New Domain / Load Domain from the Browse toolbar.
8. `src/front/templates/settings.html`
   Dropped duplicate `registry.js` include (now global).
9. Docs, domain Versions hint, UI/E2E tests updated accordingly.
10. `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-registry-modal-design.md`
    Design note for the modal entry point.

