## Fix Bridges canvas height in Registry modal

Context: After moving Bridges into the Registry modal, the graph canvas
stayed invisible even when bridges existed. Layout CSS still targeted the
old `#bridges-section` sidebar parent, so `#bridgesGraph` got zero height
and the SVG (`height: 100%`) rendered as empty.

Changes:

1. `src/front/static/global/css/registry-modal.css`
   Flex-sized the modal body / Bridges tab so the graph container receives
   a real viewport (min-height 280px).
2. `src/front/static/registry/js/registry.js`
   Re-render the D3 graph when switching to Graph view or re-entering the
   Bridges tab after a prior zero-size draw.

Modified files:
- src/front/static/global/css/registry-modal.css
- src/front/static/registry/js/registry.js

